      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Often, yes. Particulate counts that spike when the blower starts point at the duct system or the filter seal. A reading that drifts all day with the windows shut points at the house itself. Humidity that climbs only while the air conditioner runs suggests a coil or drainage problem. City & Suburban technicians are NATE-certified, and the company repairs all makes and models."
